<title>UK: Novorossiisk pipeline to shut for repair - sources.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk pipeline to shut for repair - sources.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crude oil pipelines feeding Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea will close on Thursday for 60 hours of repair, a shipping source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The closure is not likely to hinder the loading expected this week of Russian Export Blend onto the tankers Kriti Wave, Virginia Two and the Biruinta, the source said.</p>
<p>The pipelines should be up and running by the time of the arrival of the next vessel, the Agip Marche, which will load at the weekend, the source said.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea and Baltic ports were working normally on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
